{"tool_name":"muscle_ws_jabaws","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"muscle_ws_jabaws","home":"http://www.compbio.dundee.ac.uk/jabaws","summary":"Multiple sequence algnment tool.","addition_date":"2015-08-03T09:36:10Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:17:47.947650Z","tool_type":["Web service"],"version":["1"],"collections":["JABAWS","MUSCLE"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:muscle_ws_jabaws","credit":[{"name":"BioCatalogue","typeEntity":"Project","typeRole":["Documentor"],"url":"https://www.biocatalogue.org"},{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.compbio.dundee.ac.uk/jabaws/contacts.html"}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"http://www.compbio.dundee.ac.uk/jabaws/full_javadoc/compbio/ws/server/MuscleWS.html"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://www.compbio.dundee.ac.uk/jabaws/man_about.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"}}],"operation":[{"term":"Multiple sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0492"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0863"}}]}],"name":"Muscle WS (jabaws)","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"BioCatalogue","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btr304","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: JABAWS is a web services framework that simplifies the deployment of web services for bioinformatics. JABAWS:MSA provides services for five multiple sequence alignment (MSA) methods (Probcons, T-coffee, Muscle, Mafft and ClustalW), and is the system employed by the Jalview multiple sequence analysis workbench since version 2.6. A fully functional, easy to set up server is provided as a Virtual Appliance (VA), which can be run on most operating systems that support a virtualization environment such as VMware or Oracle VirtualBox. JABAWS is also distributed as a Web Application aRchive (WAR) and can be configured to run on a single computer and/or a cluster managed by Grid Engine, LSF or other queuing systems that support DRMAA. JABAWS:MSA provides clients full access to each application's parameters, allows administrators to specify named parameter preset combinations and execution limits for each application through simple configuration files. The JABAWS command-line client allows integration of JABAWS services into conventional scripts. \u00a9 The Author(s) 2011. Published by Oxford University Press.","authors":[{"name":"Barton G.J."},{"name":"Procter J.B."},{"name":"Troshin P.V."}],"citationCount":96,"date":"2011-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Java bioinformatics analysis web services for multiple sequence alignment-JABAWS:MSA"},"pmcid":"PMC3129525","pmid":"21593132","type":["Review"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Muscle WS (jabaws)","home":"https://bio.tools/muscle_ws_jabaws","version":"1","summary":"Multiple sequence algnment tool.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:muscle_ws_jabaws:1/soap/www.compbio.dundee.ac.uk","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"api":true,"manual":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":103,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"2014"},{"count":3,"year":"2013"},{"count":3,"year":"2019"},{"count":5,"year":"2015"},{"count":5,"year":"2017"},{"count":5,"year":"2018"},{"count":6,"year":"2016"},{"count":7,"year":"2020"},{"count":7,"year":"2022"},{"count":8,"year":"2023"},{"count":9,"year":"2021"},{"count":13,"year":"2025"},{"count":14,"year":"2026"},{"count":16,"year":"2024"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btr304","pmcid":"PMC3129525","pmid":"21593132","r